  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/spmh/ontologies/2024/3/SPMH/SuicideIdeation">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>Suicide Ideation</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Suicidal ideation refers to thoughts, contemplation, or fantasies about taking one's own life.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/spmh/ontologies/2024/3/SPMH/SuicidalBehaviour"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/spmh/ontologies/2024/3/SPMH/Presentation">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>Presentation</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>A technique used to share the intelligence produced.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/spmh/ontologies/2024/3/SPMH/Procedure"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/spmh/ontologies/2024/3/SPMH/Trace10">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <isFoundUsing rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/spmh/ontologies/2024/3/SPMH/LLMTraceDetection"/>
    <hasExplanation>Yes, the text conveys sentiments of sadness and loss due to the death of "dear [REDACTED]," which might be a nickname for a beloved pet or individual. It also expresses a hopeful sentiment that "Heaven became a happier place."</hasExplanation>
